WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.110
A plain page of print.

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.650
Above it hover two highlighters.

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.800
One is marked narrator.

4
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.320
The other is marked Elizabeth.

5
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.440
Elizabeth has turned down Mr Darcy.

6
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.180
Months later, she waits for news of him.

7
00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.710
Then comes one sentence: "She was humbled,

8
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.290
she was grieved; she repented,
though she hardly knew of what."

9
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.240
Both highlighters move in.

10
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.900
Both hesitate.

11
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.080
No speech marks.

12
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.020
No 'she thought'.

13
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.100
So whose voice are you reading?

14
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.910
In this mission, you'll meet a
technique called free indirect style,

15
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.630
and test what it does.

16
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.310
You'll hunt for clues
in the words themselves:

17
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.440
exclamations, questions, judgements.

18
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.070
And you'll see the
Regency world around her:

19
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.000
the militia, the manners, the letters.

20
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.200
Your mission: work out
whose voice you're reading.
